rn in colorectal neoplasia: endoscopic magnifying view</article-title><source>Endoscopy</source><year>2001</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>367</fpage><lpage>373</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11315901</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Machida</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Sano</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamamoto</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Narrow-band imaging in the diagnosis of colorectal mucosal lesions: a pilot study</article-title><source>Endoscopy</source><year>2004</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>1094</fpage><lpage>1098</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1055/s-2004-826040</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15578301</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tischendorf</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wasmuth</surname><given-names>HE</given-names></name><name><surname>Koch</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Value of magnifying chromoendoscopy and narrow band imaging (NBI) in classifying colorectal polyps: a prospective controlled study</article-title><source>Endoscopy</source><year>2007</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>1092</fpage><lpage>1096</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1055/s-2007-966781</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18072061</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hirata</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanaka</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Oka</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of microves